# Canva Automation Reference for Lucky Store Receipts

## Overview
This reference guides automated receipt card generation, asset management, and export workflows using the Canva REST API and Autofill engine for Lucky Store operations (focusing on May 2026 audit workflows).

## 1. Authentication & Credentials
- Set `CANVA_CLIENT_ID` and `CANVA_CLIENT_SECRET` in environment or `~/.hermes/.env`.
- CLI login: `canva login`

## 2. Brand Template Dataset Inspection
- Fetch brand template dataset schema via Canva REST API:
  ```bash
  curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CANVA_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
    "https://api.canva.com/v1/brand-templates/<BRAND_TEMPLATE_ID>/dataset"
  ```
- **Crucial Rule:** If the dataset returns `{}` (empty), elements were tagged in the Canva editor but *not re-published as a Brand Template*. Re-publish in Canva UI (Share → More → Brand Template → Publish).

## 3. Asset Upload (Binary Files)
- Upload binary assets (PNG/JPEG/SVG with CORS compatibility) to Canva Asset API:
  ```bash
  curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $CANVA_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" \
    --data-binary "@/path/to/receipt.jpg" \
    "https://api.canva.com/v1/assets"
  ```
- Poll upload job/asset status until ready to obtain `asset.id`.

## 4. Autofill Execution
- Create autofill job using brand template and asset IDs via Canva REST API:
  ```bash
  curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $CANVA_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "brand_template_id": "<BRAND_TEMPLATE_ID>",
      "title": "Receipt Audit - May 2026",
      "data": {
        "RECEIPT_IMAGE": {"type": "image", "asset_id": "<ASSET_ID>"},
        "AMOUNT": {"type": "text", "text": "BDT 697"}
      }
    }' \
    "https://api.canva.com/v1/autofills"
  ```

## 5. Export & Download
- Create export job:
  ```bash
  curl -s -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $CANVA_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"design_id": "<DESIGN_ID>", "format": {"type": "pdf"}}' \
    "https://api.canva.com/v1/exports"
  ```
- Poll export status and download resulting export URLs via `curl`.
